<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<resources>
    <!--
        The window behind the app, which is what shows between the launcher and the
        first composition, and which Android 12 and up also draws the splash icon
        on.

        The icon's own cream, so that on a light phone the splash and the icon are
        one surface and there is no seam between them. That means this value has to
        follow ic_launcher_background.xml, which is written by
        scripts/generate-launcher-icons.py from the logo itself — so when the logo
        changes, this changes too. LauncherIconTest holds the two together rather
        than leaving it to be noticed.

        values-night/ answers the other half: a cream window on a dark phone is the
        white flash this setting exists to prevent, and it is the reason this colour
        is separate from the icon's at all — the icon may not follow the system
        theme, and this must.
    -->
    <color name="splash_background">#F1ECE1</color>
</resources>
